The Applicant respectfully requests that this Application be screened at its Stated Capacity of 480 kW.
Wexley Distribution Center, at 8420 Corley Business Parkway, Halston, is undertaking a behind-the-meter
ground-mount and carport PV addition to offset a portion of its continuous warehouse and refrigeration
demand. The Developer of Record, Karsten Solar Development LLC, has been retained to design, permit,
construct, and file for interconnection. The Applicant notes for the record: no existing DER is installed at
the service address, and no other DER filing has been made for this site.
Correspondence regarding this Application should be directed to Emery Traskin, Development Manager,
Karsten Solar Development LLC, at the phone and email shown in Section 1, with copies to the Facilities
Manager at Wexley Distribution Center.
Section 8 — Applicant Certification and Signature
The undersigned, as authorized Developer of Record for Wexley Distribution Center, certifies that:
1.The information provided in this Application is true, accurate, and complete to the best of the
Developer's and Applicant's knowledge as of the filing date.
Alleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0231 | DIS-APP-01 | Page 4

2.The Applicant will comply with all applicable Alleniom Utilities interconnection standards, tariff
provisions, and the National Electrical Code as in effect at the time of interconnection.
3.The Applicant will not energize the proposed DER in parallel with the utility system prior to receiving
written Permission to Operate from Alleniom Utilities.
4.The Applicant will notify Alleniom Utilities of any material change to the equipment, capacity, or point of
interconnection described in this Application.
5.The inverter fleet identified in Section 5 will be configured at commissioning to hold aggregate
real-power delivery at the point of common coupling to the Stated Capacity of 480 kW — export-limited
operation.
